+Of the 500 workers read from the raw file, the 494 with a recorded age have a mean age
+of 41.3 years.
+
+Adding region-by-age fixed effects, on 281 workers, leaves the gap at -0.2071 log
+points. Blau and Kahn (2017) review why a gender gap persists in the United States.
+
+Real mean hourly wages grew 3.2 percent from 2022 to 2023, in 2023 dollars.
+
+Among prime-age workers, 28.1 percent were paid below their state's minimum wage in 2022
+and 15.8 percent in 2023, a decline of 12.3 percentage points.
+
+Mean household income is highest in the West region ($73,800).
+
+Across the states that adopted the wage policy, the estimated effect on log wages is
+0.0242 (clustered standard error 0.0083).
